LICENCE = f"""
    <h2>Rotelyx</h2>
    <p>
      The protocol, both servers and the clients are published under the
      <strong>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3</strong>. That licence
      is deliberate: it requires that anybody running a modified version as a
      network service publishes their modifications. For software whose whole
      claim is what a server cannot see, being able to read what a server is
      actually running is the point.
    </p>

    <h2>What that gives you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Run it, for any purpose.</li>
      <li>Read the source and check that a build corresponds to it. The builds
          are reproducible and the hashes are published in the repository rather
          than served from the same origin as the files they describe.</li>
      <li>Change it and share your changes, under the same licence.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Standards this implements</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Where it comes from</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Group and message encryption</td><td>MLS, RFC 9420</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Post-quantum key agreement</td><td>X-Wing, over ML-KEM-768 and X25519</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Media framing</td><td>SFrame, RFC 9605</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Transport</td><td>QUIC with TLS 1.3</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Work by other people</h2>
    <p>
      The transport is derived from iroh, whose socket layer comes from Tailscale
      and whose QUIC layer is a fork of quinn, under MIT, Apache-2.0 and
      BSD-3-Clause. It is vendored into the source rather than downloaded, and
      the full provenance, including which parts were rewritten and which were
      not, is recorded in the repository. Group encryption is OpenMLS.
    </p>
    <p>
      Rotelyx owns the policy layers and the media stack. It does not claim to
      have written a QUIC implementation.
    </p>

    <h2>The name</h2>
    <p>Rotelyx and the mark are Ideoa Labs'. The code is yours to fork; the name is not.</p>
"""


PAGES = [
